                                                                         {
                                                                             "content":  "You are an AI prompt engineer specialized in high-realism architectural image generation and image-to-image restoration workflows.\n\nYour task is to generate FOUR (4) highly detailed, production-ready prompts for a house transformation sequence.\n\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT RULES:\n- Output plain text only\n- Do NOT include explanations\n- Do NOT include JSON\n- Do NOT include markdown formatting\n- Clearly label each section exactly as instructed\n- Each prompt must be fully self-contained and ready for direct use in an image generation or image editing model\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nGLOBAL SCENE \u0026 CAMERA LOCK (APPLIES TO ALL PROMPTS)\n────────────────────────────────────\n- Vertical architectural photograph\n- Low aerial drone perspective\n- Positioned slightly above roof level\n- Gently angled downward\n- 50mm lens look\n- Shallow depth of field\n- House sharply in focus\n- Distant mountains and sky softly blurred with atmospheric haze\n- Bright, natural daylight\n- Ultra-realistic architectural photography quality\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nPROMPT 1 — IMAGE GENERATION PROMPT (RUINED HOUSE)\n────────────────────────────────────\nGenerate a completely abandoned tropical tiny house that has not been touched by humanity for over 20 years.\n\nHouse condition:\n- Extreme long-term abandonment\n- Severe structural decay and deterioration\n- Cracked and broken concrete pillars\n- Exposed rebar and damaged walls\n- Collapsed or partially missing roof sections\n- Rotten and splintered wood\n- Rusted metal elements\n- Broken or missing windows and doors\n- Balcony visibly damaged and unsafe\n- Heavy moss, vines, and vegetation aggressively growing ON the house\n- Clear signs of prolonged neglect and natural decay\n\nEnvironment:\n- The house is located in the middle of lush green rice fields\n- Terrain shows natural contours, uneven soil, and organic elevation changes\n- Rice fields are wild, overgrown, and unmaintained\n- Large broad-leaf banana trees grow naturally and chaotically near the house\n- No maintained paths, gardens, or landscaping\n- No people, animals, vehicles, or modern human activity\n\nBackground:\n- Distant mountain range behind the rice fields\n- Mountains appear softly blurred with atmospheric haze\n- Natural cloud-filled sky with realistic lighting\n\nAtmosphere:\n- Cinematic realism\n- Quiet, post-abandonment mood\n- Documentary-style decay\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nPROMPT 2 — IMAGE EDITING PROMPT (CLEAN SURROUNDINGS + PURE STRUCTURE)\n────────────────────────────────────\nEdit the provided image.\n\nTASK:\nClean the surroundings and restore the house into a raw, unfinished structural state only.\n\nSTRUCTURAL RULES:\n- Repair all columns, beams, slabs, and walls\n- Restore straight lines, clean geometry, and structural integrity\n- Remove all decay, moss, vines, rust, and damage from the house\n- Expose raw concrete and unfinished structural materials only\n- NO paint\n- NO roof installation\n- NO exterior finishes\n- NO glass, windows, doors, or decorative elements\n\nSURROUNDINGS RULES:\n- Clean the immediate surroundings of debris and overgrowth\n- Keep terrain natural and realistic\n- Do NOT add landscaping, gardens, or decorative elements\n- Banana trees remain natural and unstyled\n- Rice fields remain present but cleaned of chaos\n\nSTRICT CONSISTENCY RULES:\n- The house footprint, size, position, and orientation must remain identical\n- Do NOT add or remove rooms, floors, balconies, or extensions\n- Do NOT change camera angle, framing, or perspective\n\nResult:\nA clean construction-stage structural shell of the original house in a cleared but still natural environment.\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nPROMPT 3 — IMAGE EDITING PROMPT (FULL MODERN HOUSE RESTORATION)\n────────────────────────────────────\nEdit the provided image.\n\nTASK:\nApply a complete modern tropical architectural renovation to the existing structure.\n\nHOUSE DESIGN DETAILS:\n- Modern tropical tiny house\n- Split-level design\n- Sharp slanted shed roof\n- Clean white plaster facade\n- Warm reddish-brown wood paneling beneath the eaves\n- Elevated on white concrete pillars (stilt style)\n- Wooden wrap-around front balcony\n- Glass sliding doors with wooden frames\n- Shaded open-air relaxation space beneath with a hanging wooden swing bench\n- Semi-outdoor kitchen and dining pavilion on the right side\n- Vertical wooden slat accents\n- Modern white kitchen counter with black top\n- Wooden dining table and chairs\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- Maintain the SAME structure and footprint\n- Do NOT modify surrounding land or environment\n- NO landscaping, plants, gardens, or paths\n- Rice fields and terrain must remain unchanged\n\nResult:\nA fully renovated modern tropical house standing in an untouched environment.\n\n────────────────────────────────────\nPROMPT 4 — IMAGE EDITING PROMPT (FINAL LANDSCAPING)\n────────────────────────────────────\nEdit the provided image.\n\nTASK:\nApply excellent, realistic landscaping that blends naturally with the environment.\n\nLANDSCAPING DETAILS:\n- Neatly organized vegetable garden in the foreground\n- Central gray gravel pathway leading to the house\n- Symmetrical raised planting beds\n- Young green crops bordered with small orange marigolds\n- Landscaping that feels natural, sustainable, and location-appropriate\n- Subtle refinement of banana trees without over-styling\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- The house must remain COMPLETELY unchanged\n- Do NOT alter architecture, colors, materials, or structure\n- Enhance landscape only\n\nATMOSPHERE:\n- Bright, sunny daylight\n- Balanced shadows and highlights\n- Peaceful, cinematic countryside mood"
                                                                         }
                                                                     ]
